{
  "_comment": "Playable characters. Chris and Sheva and their first skins are open from the start; every other character and skin is earned (unlock_kind/unlock_count/unlock_text/unlock_character/unlock_boss, see core/include/rm/characters.h; a character's first skin comes with it). starting_weapons: the first entry is the pistol every run starts with (the adapter strips the game's own Mercenaries loadout down to it); other weapons come from supply perks, rewards and the shop. starting_passive is the character's free style trait; skill_pool lists the perks the character can unlock. A skin is a build (ROADMAP M8, written by scripts/write_perks.py): 'build' holds its rules (weapon filters, damage by weapon category, supplies, free shop rerolls, rarity, uncapped upgrades, a starting weapon, max health), and a skin without one yet keeps a small trait (a 'skin' perk). costume_index is the class and the model each slot loads, checked in game: 0..2 and 10 Heavy Metal, 14 Warrior Chris; 3 and 11 Fairy Tale, 15 Business Sheva; 9 Wesker S.T.A.R.S.; 12 Josh, 13 Excella, 16 Barry, 17 Rebecca. Text shown by the game font: letters, digits, space, comma and period only. A skin with 'mod' wears a third-party mod's look (name, author, url: its page; files: the archives read from RogueMercenaries\\mods instead of the game's, with the size checked); without the mod it is listed but not selectable.",
